                             System Errors
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

If you encounter errors during startup of system, you can locate errors
told by the bbs system here.



Node error messages
-------------------

init node error 1
*****************
A parameter in your node setup is missing.
To start a node correctly for use with a serial driver, you must at least set:

MODEM_ANSWER
SERIAL_DRIVER
SERIAL_UNIT
SERIAL_BAUD
CONNECT_ID
CARRIERWAIT


init node error 2
*****************
Node could not initialize your serial driver, or driver name is not correct.
Note that SERIAL_DRIVER string is case-sensitive, you must write the driver
name exactly as its said when you take a "version" on the driver.
internal serial driver is called : serial.device
you must write it as written above, all letters in lower-case, to make it
work.


init node error 3
*****************
Node was unable to open timer unit, you have either a defective device
or incorrupt memory, try and reset you computer, and restart system.


init node error 4
*****************
Node was unable to open message ports needed to run node,
system message ports may have been corrupted or your memory is incorrupt,
 try and reset you computer, and restart system.


FONT ERROR
**********
Node could not locate the font specified in your setup.
You have either specified a font type which is not 8 by height or the font
is not found in your FONTS: directory.


ScreenOpen error
****************
You are low on system CHIP memory, please close unnessesary programs which
takes up CHIP memory.


TERMINATED!
***********
If you receive this message below the action information. Current node
is terminated due to an error. If you do not receive a system closedown
within 30 seconds, you must reset the system yourself, otherwise you might
 get several other errors until you reset system.



AT-CMD Error
************
If you receive this message in the username corner, at command sent to modem
for this node failed, and returned ERROR.



Other errors may occur, you can look these up , in the DEBUGLOG file.
All file errors will be written to this log file.

